1. Definitions

   "Software" means the Talyx source code in this repository and the
   binaries built from it (including the `talyx` and `talyx-shim`
   programs), but not the third-party components listed in
   THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, which are covered by their own licenses.

   "We" / "us" means the copyright holder named above. "You" means the
   person or entity using the Software.

   "License Key" means an activation key we (or an authorized reseller)
   issue to you, that has not expired or been revoked, and whose seat count
   you have not exceeded.

   "Enforcement Features" means any function of the Software that modifies
   another program's configuration or mediates its execution — including
   `talyx init`, `talyx allow`, and the `talyx-shim` gate.
   The read-only reporting commands (`talyx scan`, `talyx status`,
   `talyx why`, `talyx guardrails`, `talyx advisories`) are
   not Enforcement Features.

2. What you may do without a License Key

   We grant you a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable
   right to:

   (a) download, view, and compile the Software;

   (b) run the Software for security review, evaluation, and testing; and

   (c) run the read-only reporting commands for any purpose, including
       commercially.

3. What requires a License Key

   Running the Enforcement Features, other than briefly to evaluate them,
   requires a valid License Key for each developer who uses them. The
   commercial terms you accept when you obtain a License Key govern that
   use alongside this license; if they conflict, those terms control for
   License Key holders.

